Presidential elections were held in [[Lithuania]] on 12 May 2024, alongside a [[2024 Lithuanian constitutional referendum|referendum on allowing multiple citizenships]].<ref name=LRT>{{cite web|url=https://www.lrt.lt/en/news-in-english/19/1995960/lithuania-to-hold-multiple-citizenship-referendum-in-2024|title=Lithuania to hold multiple citizenship referendum in 2024|website=LRT|date=23 May 2023|access-date=14 December 2023|archive-date=27 January 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240127121743/https://www.lrt.lt/en/news-in-english/19/1995960/lithuania-to-hold-multiple-citizenship-referendum-in-2024|url-status=live}}</ref> Incumbent President [[Gitanas Nausėda]] won re-election to a second term. When candidate registrations closed before the election, the {{ill|Lithuanian Central Election Commission|lt|Vyriausioji rinkimų komisija}} had confirmed fifteen viable registrations; of those, twelve proceeded to [[Nomination rules|collect signatures]] from the minimum 20,000 voters. Four of those contenders were later repudiated or dropped out,<ref>{{cite news | last=Vaišvilaitė-Braziulienė | first=Justina | title=Eight candidates to vie for president – election watchdog | work=Delfi | date=8 April 2024 | url=https://www.delfi.lt/en/politics/eight-candidates-to-vie-for-president-election-watchdog-96308707 | language=lt | access-date=9 April 2024 | archive-date=9 April 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240409155203/https://www.delfi.lt/en/politics/eight-candidates-to-vie-for-president-election-watchdog-96308707 | url-status=live }}</ref> leaving eight on the [[ballot]].<ref name="EL9">{{cite news |title=VRK registravo likusius kandidatus prezidento rinkimams: dėl šalies vadovo posto varžysis 8 politikai |url=https://www.lrytas.lt/lietuvosdiena/aktualijos/2024/04/09/news/vrk-registravo-likusius-kandidatus-prezidento-rinkimams-del-salies-vadovo-posto-varzysis-8-politikai-31339272 |access-date=9 April 2024 |work=Lietuvos rytas |agency=ELTA |date=9 April 2024 |language=lt |archive-date=27 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240527185257/https://www.lrytas.lt/lietuvosdiena/aktualijos/2024/04/09/news/vrk-registravo-likusius-kandidatus-prezidento-rinkimams-del-salies-vadovo-posto-varzysis-8-politikai-31339272 |url-status=live }}</ref> 

A second round was held on 26 May as no candidate received an absolute majority in the first round.<ref name="ap">{{Cite web |title=Lithuanians vote in a presidential election as anxieties rise over Russia and the war in Ukraine |url=https://apnews.com/article/lithuania-presidential-election-gitanas-nauseda-fcb8f81f23033f63ce780b1ffe477185 |access-date=12 May 2024 |website=Associated Press |date=12 May 2024 |archive-date=27 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240527185257/https://apnews.com/article/lithuania-presidential-election-gitanas-nauseda-fcb8f81f23033f63ce780b1ffe477185 |url-status=live }}</ref> This saw Nausėda and Prime Minister [[Ingrida Šimonytė]] facing off in the runoff, a rematch of the [[2019 Lithuanian presidential election|2019 election]] in which Nausėda had defeated Šimonytė. Nausėda won re-election, defeating Šimonytė in a second-round landslide with 75% of the vote – the largest margin of victory in a free election for any presidential candidate in the history of Lithuania.

==Background==
{{main article|President of Lithuania}}
The Lithuanian president has somewhat more executive authority than their counterparts in neighboring [[president of Estonia|Estonia]] and [[president of Latvia|Latvia]]; the Lithuanian president's function is similar to that of the presidents of [[President of France|France]] and [[President of Romania|Romania]]. Similarly to them, but unlike presidents in a fully presidential system such as [[President of the United States|the United States]], the Lithuanian president generally has the most authority in [[foreign affairs]]. In addition to the customary diplomatic powers of [[heads of state]], namely receiving the [[letters of credence]] of foreign ambassadors and signing [[treaties]], the president determines Lithuania's basic foreign policy guidelines. The president is also the [[commander-in-chief]] of the [[Lithuanian Armed Forces]], and accordingly heads the State Defense Council and has the right to appoint the [[Chief of Defence (Lithuania)|Chief of Defence]] (subject to Seimas consent).<ref name="Powers">{{Cite web |url=https://www.lrp.lt/en/institution/presidential-functions/35145 |title=Presidential Functions {{!}} President of the Republic of Lithuania |access-date=7 April 2024 |archive-date=25 December 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211225160609/https://www.lrp.lt/en/institution/presidential-functions/35145 |url-status=live }}</ref>

The president has a significant role in domestic policy, possessing the right to submit bills to the [[Seimas]] and to [[veto]] laws passed by it, appointing the [[Prime Minister of Lithuania|prime minister]] and approving the government formed by them, and also having the right to [[Dissolution of Parliament|dissolve]] the Seimas and call [[snap elections]] following a successful [[motion of no confidence]] or if the Seimas refuses to approve the government's budget within sixty days. However, the next elected Seimas may retaliate by calling for an earlier presidential election.<ref name="Constitution">{{Cite web |url=https://e-seimas.lrs.lt/portal/legalAct/lt/TAD/TAIS.21892?jfwid=-wd7z8ivg5 |title=Constitution of the Republic of Lithuania – Seimas site |access-date=7 April 2024 |archive-date=25 December 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211225160604/https://e-seimas.lrs.lt/portal/legalAct/lt/TAD/TAIS.21892?jfwid=-wd7z8ivg5 |url-status=live }}</ref> In addition, according to a resolution by the [[Constitutional Court of Lithuania]] in 1998, the president is required by law to nominate the candidate of the parliamentary majority to the office of prime minister.<ref name="galios">{{cite web |last1=Jastramskis |first1=Mažvydas |title=Ką gali Lietuvos prezidentas? |url=https://www.prezidentogalios.lt/ka-gali-lietuvos-prezidentas |website=Prezidentogalios.lt |language=lt |date=3 April 2024 |access-date=7 April 2024 |archive-date=27 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240527185258/https://www.prezidentogalios.lt/ka-gali-lietuvos-prezidentas |url-status=live }}</ref>

The president also holds informal power, as the office of president is generally more trusted by the populace according to approval polling, and Lithuanian presidents historically blocked legislation and forced the resignation of prime ministers (such as [[Gediminas Vagnorius]] in 1998).<ref name="galios" />

==Electoral system==
The president is elected using the [[two-round system]]. To win in the first round, a candidate requires an absolute majority of all votes cast (including invalid votes) and either voter turnout to be above 50% or for their vote share to be equivalent to at least one-third of the number of registered voters. If no candidate wins in the first round, a second round is required, featuring the top two candidates. All candidates for president are [[Independent (politician)|independent]]. While some candidates belong to and/or are supported by a [[political party]], the office of the president is formally non-partisan.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.electionguide.org/elections/id/3146/|title=Lithuania: Election for President|website=IFES Election Guide|access-date=7 October 2023|archive-date=10 August 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200810085209/https://www.electionguide.org/elections/id/3146/|url-status=live}}</ref>

Citizens of Lithuania at least 40 years of age whose at least one parent was also a citizen ([[natural-born-citizen clause]]), who have lived in Lithuania for at least three years prior, are not serving a [[Imprisonment|prison sentence]], are not on [[active duty]] in the [[Lithuanian Armed Forces]], are not bound to any other country by an [[oath]] and have never been [[impeachment|impeached]], are allowed to run for president. Each candidate must collect at least 20 thousand signatures by Lithuanian citizens to be able to run for election.<ref>{{cite web |title=Lietuvos Respublikos Prezidentas |url=https://www.vle.lt/straipsnis/lietuvos-respublikos-prezidentas/ |website=[[Visuotinė lietuvių enciklopedija]] |language=Lithuanian |access-date=24 October 2023 |archive-date=27 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240527190216/https://www.vle.lt/straipsnis/lietuvos-respublikos-prezidentas/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news | last=Andrukaitytė | first=Milena | title=VRK patvirtino, kad Šimonytė surinko parašus prezidento rinkimams | work=LRT | date=7 March 2024 | url=https://www.lrt.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/2/2216459/vrk-patvirtino-kad-simonyte-surinko-parasus-prezidento-rinkimams | language=lt | access-date=27 March 2024 | archive-date=27 May 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240527190611/https://www.lrt.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/2/2216459/vrk-patvirtino-kad-simonyte-surinko-parasus-prezidento-rinkimams | url-status=live }}</ref>

==Candidates==
All pre-registered candidates were required to finalize the registration procedure by 8 March 2024, in order to commence the collection of signatures for the confirmation of their candidacy. Ten out of 15 candidates completed this before the start of the procurement phase.<ref name=";21" /> Two candidates managed to resolve it afterwards. [[#Pre-registered|Three other aspirants]] chose against launching a presidential bid or were eliminated due to the failure to complete the procedure before the deadline.<ref name="two+one" />

All declared candidates for president had to gather 20,000 signatures physically or online in order to be registered and present them by 28 March 2024 at {{UTZ|17:00|EET}}.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Jurčenkaitė |first1=Indrė |title=L.Matjošaitytė: parašų rinkimas prezidento rinkimuose gerina rekordus |url=https://www.15min.lt/naujiena/aktualu/lietuva/l-matjosaityte-parasu-rinkimas-prezidento-rinkimuose-gerina-rekordus-56-1105518 |work=15min |language=lt |date=2019-02-20 |access-date=18 October 2023 |archive-date=27 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240527190614/https://www.15min.lt/naujiena/aktualu/lietuva/l-matjosaityte-parasu-rinkimas-prezidento-rinkimuose-gerina-rekordus-56-1105518 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Politinės kampanijos dalyviai |url=https://www.vrk.lt/politines-kampanijos-dalyviai-2024-pr?srcUrl=/politKamp/1644/dalyviai/dalyviai.html |website=Central Electoral Commission of Lithuania |language=Lithuanian |date=2024 |access-date=22 January 2024 |archive-date=4 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240204111453/https://www.vrk.lt/politines-kampanijos-dalyviai-2024-pr?srcUrl=/politKamp/1644/dalyviai/dalyviai.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Four [[#Registered|failed or dropped out]] in the process,<ref name="Die0">{{cite news | title=VRK baigė tikrinti kandidatų į prezidentus surinktus rinkėjų parašus: sąraše – aštuoni kandidatai | work=DIENA.lt | date=2024-04-08 | url=https://www.diena.lt/naujienos/lietuva/politika/vrk-baige-tikrinti-kandidatu-i-prezidentus-surinktus-rinkeju-parasus-sarase-8-kandidatai-1168720 | language=lt | access-date=2024-04-08 | archive-date=8 April 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240408190451/https://www.diena.lt/naujienos/lietuva/politika/vrk-baige-tikrinti-kandidatu-i-prezidentus-surinktus-rinkeju-parasus-sarase-8-kandidatai-1168720 | url-status=live }}</ref> so the following eight candidates appeared on the [[ballot]] on 12 May.<ref name="EL9" /><ref name="table-ref">{{cite web |title=Kandidatai į Respublikos Prezidentus |url=https://www.vrk.lt/en/kandidatai-i-respublikos-prezidentus-2024-pr |publisher=Central Electoral Commission |access-date=12 April 2024 |language=lt}}</ref>

