==Campaign==
Incumbent President [[Gitanas Nausėda]] sought re-election against a range of opponents including [[Ingrida Šimonytė]], his runoff challenger in the [[2019 Lithuanian presidential election]] and incumbent [[Prime Minister of Lithuania]]. After announcing his bid on 7 December 2023, Nausėda became the clear frontrunner,<ref>{{cite web |last1=Valiauskaitė |first1=Aistė |title='Eurovision for politicians': Lithuania's 2024 presidential election holds little suspense |url=https://www.lrt.lt/en/news-in-english/19/2160069/eurovision-for-politicians-lithuania-s-2024-presidential-election-holds-little-suspense |website=LRT |language=Lithuanian |date=2 January 2024 |access-date=17 January 2024 |archive-date=17 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240117114205/https://www.lrt.lt/en/news-in-english/19/2160069/eurovision-for-politicians-lithuania-s-2024-presidential-election-holds-little-suspense |url-status=live }}</ref> while Šimonytė was the sole [[woman]] vying for the presidency. Former chairman of the Lithuanian Bar Association [[Ignas Vėgėlė]] was considered to be an [[anti-establishment]] candidate,<ref name=":2" /><ref>{{cite web |title=LRT forumas 2024-04-15 |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9An0ma0AeHg |website=YouTube |publisher=LRT |access-date=16 April 2024 |date=15 April 2024 |archive-date=16 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240416221952/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9An0ma0AeHg |url-status=live }}</ref> although several candidates contended for the [[protest vote]].<ref>{{cite news | last=Gaučaitė-Znutienė | first=Modesta | title=Intriga – ne laimėtojas, o kas mes iššūkį antrame ture: Nausėdą erzintų ne Šimonytė, o Vėgėlės šešėlis | work=LRT | date=26 February 2024 | url=https://www.lrt.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/2/2200702/intriga-ne-laimetojas-o-kas-mes-issuki-antrame-ture-nauseda-erzintu-ne-simonyte-o-vegeles-seselis | language=lt | access-date=9 April 2024 | archive-date=9 April 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240409155203/https://www.lrt.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/2/2200702/intriga-ne-laimetojas-o-kas-mes-issuki-antrame-ture-nauseda-erzintu-ne-simonyte-o-vegeles-seselis | url-status=live }}</ref> [[Eduardas Vaitkus]] was regarded as the pro-Russian candidate in the election and received support from the [[Poles in Lithuania|Polish]]-majority [[Šalčininkai]] region and [[Visaginas]], which is predominantly inhabited by [[Russians in Lithuania|ethnic Russians]].<ref>{{cite news | title=Lithuania's president set for runoff in re-election bid amid security concerns | work=TVP | date=13 May 2024 | url=https://tvpworld.com/77498573/lithuanias-president-set-for-runoff-in-re-election-bid-amid-security-concerns | access-date=14 May 2024 | archive-date=14 May 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240514054625/https://tvpworld.com/77498573/lithuanias-president-set-for-runoff-in-re-election-bid-amid-security-concerns | url-status=live }}</ref>

National security in the aftermath of the [[Russian invasion of Ukraine]] and the financing of the [[Lithuanian Armed Forces|military]], universal [[conscription]],<ref>{{cite web |last1=Broga |first1=Karolis |title=Universal conscription has become election issue, says LVŽS leader |url=https://www.delfi.lt/en/politics/universal-conscription-has-become-election-issue-says-lvzs-leader-95541457 |website=Delfi |language=Lithuanian |date=5 January 2024 |access-date=17 January 2024 |archive-date=17 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240117114205/https://www.delfi.lt/en/politics/universal-conscription-has-become-election-issue-says-lvzs-leader-95541457 |url-status=live }}</ref> managing effects of the [[Ageing of Europe|ageing population]], [[cost of living]],<ref>{{cite web |last1=Bakaitė |first1=Jurga |title=Veryga skelbia, koks būtų prezidentas: pažadėjo ginti "tradicines vertybes" |url=https://www.lrt.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/2/2146900/veryga-skelbia-koks-butu-prezidentas-pazadejo-ginti-tradicines-vertybes |website=LRT |language=Lithuanian |date=11 December 2023 |quote=A. Veryga sakė matantis, kad dauguma gyventojų nusivylė dabartine valdžia.  „Aš matau, kad dauguma gyventojų nusivylė ir nurašė dabartinės politikos formuotojus. Pasitikėjimas Vyriausybe yra rekordinėse žemumose. Piliečių nuomonė ignoruojama. Mūsų žmonės vis rečiau pasiryžta kurti šeimas. Pamažu nykstame kaip valstybė", – sakė jis. |access-date=17 January 2024 |archive-date=17 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240117114205/https://www.lrt.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/2/2146900/veryga-skelbia-koks-butu-prezidentas-pazadejo-ginti-tradicines-vertybes |url-status=live }}</ref> the [[One China|One China Policy]],<ref>{{cite news | title=Concern about Russia dominates as Lithuanians vote | work=VOA | date=12 May 2024 | url=https://www.voanews.com/a/concern-about-russia-dominates-as-lithuanians-vote-/7607770.html | access-date=13 May 2024 | archive-date=13 May 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240513050607/https://www.voanews.com/a/concern-about-russia-dominates-as-lithuanians-vote-/7607770.html | url-status=live }}</ref> ratification of the [[Istanbul Convention]], Nausėda's 2019 presidential campaign and [[Gitanas Nausėda#The Whistleblower and the President|alleged connections]] with business interests from [[Russia]] and [[Belarus]],<ref>{{cite news | last=Jakučionis | first=Saulius | title=Parliament commission indicts Lithuanian president in 'whistleblower case' | work=LRT | date=26 March 2024 | url=https://www.lrt.lt/en/news-in-english/19/2234671/parliament-commission-indicts-lithuanian-president-in-whistleblower-case | access-date=11 April 2024 | archive-date=5 April 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240405180021/https://www.lrt.lt/en/news-in-english/19/2234671/parliament-commission-indicts-lithuanian-president-in-whistleblower-case | url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news | last=Voveriūnaitė | first=Simona | title=Nausėdos situacija primena 20 metų senumo istoriją: ekspertas išskyrė skirtumus | work=Delfi | date=6 April 2024 | url=https://www.delfi.lt/news/daily/politics/nausedos-situacija-primena-20-metu-senumo-istorija-ekspertas-isskyre-skirtumus-96286255 | language=lt | access-date=11 April 2024 | archive-date=6 April 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240406105205/https://www.delfi.lt/news/daily/politics/nausedos-situacija-primena-20-metu-senumo-istorija-ekspertas-isskyre-skirtumus-96286255 | url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news | last=Gaučaitė-Znutienė | first=Modesta | title=Bakas tikina, kad Nausėdos aplinkoje buvo dešimtys su Rusija ir Baltarusija susijusių žmonių | work=LRT | date=27 March 2024 | url=https://www.lrt.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/2/2235323/bakas-tikina-kad-nausedos-aplinkoje-buvo-desimtys-su-rusija-ir-baltarusija-susijusiu-zmoniu | language=lt | access-date=11 April 2024 | archive-date=5 April 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240405180042/https://www.lrt.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/2/2235323/bakas-tikina-kad-nausedos-aplinkoje-buvo-desimtys-su-rusija-ir-baltarusija-susijusiu-zmoniu | url-status=live }}</ref> the [[Šimonytė Cabinet]]<ref name=":2">{{cite web |title=Politologė kandidato į prezidentus Vėgėlės retorikoje įžvelgia populizmą: gelbės tautą nuo "piktojo elito" |url=https://www.lrt.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/2/2139694/politologe-kandidato-i-prezidentus-vegeles-retorikoje-izvelgia-populizma-gelbes-tauta-nuo-piktojo-elito |website=LRT |language=Lithuanian |date=1 December 2023 |access-date=17 January 2024 |archive-date=17 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240117114206/https://www.lrt.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/2/2139694/politologe-kandidato-i-prezidentus-vegeles-retorikoje-izvelgia-populizma-gelbes-tauta-nuo-piktojo-elito |url-status=live }}</ref> and its conflict with Nausėda<ref>{{cite web |title=Ingrida Šimonytė teigia, kad būtų kitokia prezidentė nei Gitanas Nausėda |url=https://ve.lt/gyvenimas/ingrida-simonyte-teigia-kad-butu-kitokia-prezidente-nei-gitanas-nauseda |website=Vakarų ekspresas |language=Lithuanian |date=4 November 2023 |access-date=17 January 2024 |archive-date=17 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240117181300/https://ve.lt/gyvenimas/ingrida-simonyte-teigia-kad-butu-kitokia-prezidente-nei-gitanas-nauseda |url-status=live }}</ref> emerged as potential leading issues during the campaign. Both Nausėda and Šimonytė agreed on increasing defense spending and strengthening relations with [[NATO]], but diverged on other issues such as economic policy and [[Recognition of same-sex unions in Lithuania|same-sex unions]], which Nausėda opposes.<ref name="facebook"/><ref>{{cite news | title=Lithuanians go to polls in presidential election | work=TVP | date=12 May 2024 | url=https://tvpworld.com/77486738/lithuanians-go-to-polls-in-presidential-election | access-date=14 May 2024 | archive-date=14 May 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240514054625/https://tvpworld.com/77486738/lithuanians-go-to-polls-in-presidential-election | url-status=live }}</ref> Both candidates also shared diverging views on the [[Taiwanese Representative Office in Lithuania]], whose naming after the island rather than the standard practice of using its capital [[Taipei]] led to diplomatic and economic sanctions from China. Nausėda supports having the office change its name, which Šimonytė opposes.<ref name="facebook"/>

Following the results of the first round, Nausėda expressed thanks to the Lithuanian people for their support during his five years in office despite challenges such as inequality, while Šimonytė said the results indicated support for her premiership. Ignas Vėgėlė attributed his defeat to the distribution of votes among the candidates who campaigned on a change platform and his lack of political experience.<ref>{{cite news | title=Nausėda and Šimonytė make it to runoffs in rerun of 2019 presidential election | work=LRT | date=13 May 2024 | url=https://www.lrt.lt/en/news-in-english/19/2270543/nauseda-and-simonyte-make-it-to-runoffs-in-rerun-of-2019-presidential-election | access-date=14 May 2024 | archive-date=14 May 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240514051554/https://www.lrt.lt/en/news-in-english/19/2270543/nauseda-and-simonyte-make-it-to-runoffs-in-rerun-of-2019-presidential-election | url-status=live }}</ref>

===Candidate donations and funding===
[[Campaign finance|Campaign funding]] in elections in Lithuania is heavily restricted. The maximum amount each candidate is limited to raise is €2 million. Only [[Person|individuals]] living in Lithuania and registered political parties may provide funding for a candidate. The candidate themselves may contribute a maximum of €36,000 or one fifth of their total declared income and assets. Individuals who had yet to declare income can only donate up to €50 through the entire electoral cycle, whereas individuals who had done so may contribute a maximum of €18,000 or one tenth of their total declared income and assets.{{cn|date=May 2024}}

The system has been criticized for providing for a handicapped, monotonous campaign and diluting the chance of unknown candidates to spread their message to wider, untapped audiences.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Vilikanskytė |first1=Milda |title=Nuo savo kišenės iki verslininkų: kas remia kandidatus prezidento rinkimuose |url=https://www.lrt.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/2/2240662/nuo-savo-kisenes-iki-verslininku-kas-remia-kandidatus-i-prezidento-rinkimuose |website=LRT |language=lt |date=2 April 2024 |access-date=2 April 2024 |archive-date=2 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240402232347/https://www.lrt.lt/naujienos/lietuvoje/2/2240662/nuo-savo-kisenes-iki-verslininku-kas-remia-kandidatus-i-prezidento-rinkimuose |url-status=live }}</ref>

