==Aftermath==
Following the release of the election results for the second round, Šimonytė conceded defeat,<ref name="ajvictory">{{Cite web |title=Lithuania's Gitanas Nauseda declares victory in presidential election |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/5/26/lithuanias-gitanas-nauseda-declares-victory-in-presidential-election |access-date=2024-05-27 |website=Al Jazeera |language=en |archive-date=27 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240527060010/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/5/26/lithuanias-gitanas-nauseda-declares-victory-in-presidential-election |url-status=live }}</ref> and said that she would continue in office as prime minister. Nausėda acknowledged that the electorate had given him their mandate and said that he "will have to cherish this credit of trust". Final turnout was estimated at 49.61%.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Nausėda claims landslide victory in Lithuania's presidential run-off |url=https://www.lrt.lt/en/news-in-english/19/2278660/presidential-election-run-off-underway-in-lithuania |access-date=2024-05-27 |website=LRT |date=27 May 2024 |language=en |archive-date=26 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240526043625/https://www.lrt.lt/en/news-in-english/19/2278660/presidential-election-run-off-underway-in-lithuania |url-status=live }}</ref>

==Reactions==
Polish President [[Andrzej Duda]] congratulated Nausėda on his reelection and said he was "pleased that we'll be able to continue our excellent cooperation".<ref>{{Cite web |title=Polish president congratulates Lithuanian counterpart on re-election |url=https://tvpworld.com/77755290/polish-president-congratulates-lithuanian-counterpart-on-reelection |access-date=2024-05-27 |website=TVP |date=27 May 2024 |language=en |archive-date=27 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240527093013/https://tvpworld.com/77755290/polish-president-congratulates-lithuanian-counterpart-on-reelection |url-status=live }}</ref> Ukrainian President [[Volodymyr Zelenskyy]] also expressed his congratulations to Nausėda, citing the latter's support for Ukraine amid the Russian invasion.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Lithuania's incumbent president declares victory in runoff vote |url=https://kyivindependent.com/nauseda-claims-landslide-victory-in-lithuanian-presidential-election/ |access-date=2024-05-27 |website=The Kyiv Independent |date=27 May 2024 |language=en |archive-date=27 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240527072901/https://kyivindependent.com/nauseda-claims-landslide-victory-in-lithuanian-presidential-election/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

